                "copied. Figure G2.1 redraws the lecture's board sketch of paths approaching $(a,b)$.<br><b>Class "
                '002.</b> Colours follow the Okabe–Ito order: blue = main curve, vermilion = comparison or tangent, '
                'green = second trace, purple = other direction. Tangents are dashed. Grey dashed lines are '
                'references. The surfaces (dome $z=4-x^2-y^2$, saddle $z=x^2-y^2$, $z=x^2y$) are illustrative choices '
